#
# The flagship acceptance manifest — the epic's depth bar as a typed contract.
#
# The mathematics grounding layer's depth is defined by five flagship acceptance
# scenarios, not by adjectives. Each is realized by a worked example, pinned by a
# competency question, and guarded by a counter-example that raises a named failure
# class. This manifest reifies the acceptance bar ITSELF: five math:FlagshipScenario
# individuals, each binding one scenario to the four artifacts that realize and enforce
# it —
#   math:demonstratedByExample     → the worked examples/*.ttl
#   math:demonstratedByCompetency  → the gmeow:CompetencyQuestion that pins it
#   math:guardedByCounterExample   → the minimal violation that proves the gate bites
#   math:enforcesFailureClass      → the math:MathConformanceFailure subclass it raises
#
# The bindings are gated across three surfaces: SHACL (math:FlagshipScenarioShape) and
# a structural ASK (ex:saFlagshipCoverage) check that the five are present and fully
# linked with a real failure class; the native flagship cross-check resolves each
# math:demonstratedByCompetency into tests/competency.ttl and confirms it carries a
# gmeow:cqExpectRow expectation and an existing query file. The competency-question
# individuals live in the tests dataset, which SHACL never loads — hence the split.
# Validates cleanly.

@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix exa:  <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/acceptance/> .
@prefix cq:   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/math/tests/> .

# --- Flagship 1 — the symmetry groups of E8 -------------------------------- #
exa:e8Symmetry a math:FlagshipScenario ;
    rdfs:label "Flagship: the symmetry groups of E8"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "Lie group and Lie algebra, root system (240 roots in rank 8), Weyl group modelled as the automorphism group preserving the root system, its numbers pinned by an exact-match competency gate."@x-gmeow-english ;
    math:demonstratedByExample "examples/e8-symmetry.ttl" ;
    math:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqE8RootSystem ;
    math:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/e8-wrong-weyl-order.ttl" ;
    math:enforcesFailureClass math:WrongE8WeylOrder .

# --- Flagship 2 — how homomorphic encryption works ------------------------- #
exa:homomorphicEncryption a math:FlagshipScenario ;
    rdfs:label "Flagship: how homomorphic encryption works"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A ring homomorphism whose homomorphic law (Dec(E(a) ⊗ E(b)) = a ⊕ b) is a logic: formula grounded in math: ring/lattice structure, framed by its noise model and security assumption."@x-gmeow-english ;
    math:demonstratedByExample "examples/homomorphic-encryption.ttl" ;
    math:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqHeSchemeFrame ;
    math:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/he-scheme-missing-noise-model.ttl" ;
    math:enforcesFailureClass math:UnderspecifiedEncryptionScheme .

# --- Flagship 3 — complex proofs as process -------------------------------- #
exa:proofAsProcess a math:FlagshipScenario ;
    rdfs:label "Flagship: complex proofs as process"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A proof effort as a goal-decomposed process whose QED is a verification observation grounded in a vantage — the proof-dependency DAG lifted through the bridge, with an ungrounded verdict rejected."@x-gmeow-english ;
    math:demonstratedByExample "examples/bridges.ttl" ;
    math:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqBridgeProof ;
    math:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/verification-result-ungrounded.ttl" ;
    math:enforcesFailureClass math:UngroundedVerificationResult .

# --- Flagship 4 — the universal R → math: bridge --------------------------- #
exa:rBridge a math:FlagshipScenario ;
    rdfs:label "Flagship: R → math:, for any R script"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A universal lift where an R script's mathematical/statistical content lifts into math: as the put leg of a logic:Correspondence, hard-failing with a typed diagnostic on anything it cannot lift rather than dropping it silently."@x-gmeow-english ;
    math:demonstratedByExample "examples/bridges.ttl" ;
    math:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqBridgeRFidelity ;
    math:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/ingest-run-unliftable.ttl" ;
    math:enforcesFailureClass math:UnliftableIngest .

# --- Flagship 5 — an AI describing its own structure ----------------------- #
exa:aiSelfStructure a math:FlagshipScenario ;
    rdfs:label "Flagship: an AI describing its own structure"@x-gmeow-english ;
    skos:definition "A tensor computational graph as a math: object, weights as matrices in a parameter space, embeddings as latent-space geometry with residual meaning, and the AI's reflection carried at the logic: metalevel — the dogfooding apex."@x-gmeow-english ;
    math:demonstratedByExample "examples/linear-algebra-and-learning.ttl" ;
    math:demonstratedByCompetency cq:cqTensorGraph ;
    math:guardedByCounterExample "tests/counter-examples/tensor-graph-no-node.ttl" ;
    math:enforcesFailureClass math:MalformedTensorComputationGraph .
